            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0227" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4722: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-10T22:00:00-04:00">November 10,
                            1943—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7089. With reference to your number 7565, November 1, Department is unable to see
                    how benefits derived from informing other governments of proposed declaration on
                    repatriation prior to having approval of the Soviet Government would justify
                    incurring possible displeasure of Soviet authorities should they disapprove the
                    declaration. Department believes declaration will be of little value unless
                    accepted by Soviet Government and is requesting American Ambassador at Moscow to
                    endeavor to expedite Soviet reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
